To upgrade the [[Dull Dagger]] into [[Keeper of the Crimson Covenant]], you need to do the following:

1. Equip [[Dull Dagger]] on a character that has [[Follower of the Blood of Vol]]; the [[Dull Dagger]] gains {{Popup|Lesser Favor of the Lady Vol|"I will reward your faith."}}.  Other methods of turning daggers into Favored Weapons, such as Divine Crusader, do not count. '''Important Note:''' If you equip [[Dull Dagger]] on a character without [[Follower of the Blood of Vol]] before ''fully'' upgrading it, it will lose {{Popup|Lesser Favor of the Lady Vol|"I will reward your faith."}} and you will need to give it this lesser upgrade again before you can fully upgrade it.

2. While wielding [[Dull Dagger]] with {{Popup|Lesser Favor of the Lady Vol|"I will reward your faith."}}, enter [[Mark of Death]] and step into the blue mist, which gives you the "Manifest Zone: Dolurrh" debuff. 

The dagger is now fully upgraded, and you will have a [[Keeper of the Crimson Covenant]] of your very own. Once fully upgraded, this knife persists through reincarnation, and you can equip it on any (Level 29+) character, regardless of their faith.

Further Information: "While I was upgrading my Dull Dagger, I stepped into and out of the Manifest Zones of Dolurrh multiple times without the dagger upgrading. I had previously been disjunctioned by the Abbot and that effect had not worn off yet. The Disjunction temporarily removed the 'I will reward your faith...' effect and with that not on the dagger, it would not upgrade. Once the disjunction wore off, I stepped into the manifest zone once and it instantly upgraded. Keep an eye out for the disjunction if you plan on keeping the dagger equipped in the earlier parts of the raid, or only equip the dagger after the manifest zones begin appearing to avoid this issue." 
